e{ln}⁡(5)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) & =7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6) \\\\ 4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-7x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6) & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ x(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)) & =5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5) \\\\ x & =\\frac{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-7\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264595 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264596 13194139533900 true] [17592186264595 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533900 true] [17592186264595 1041 "field-1" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264595 1104 #edb/ref 17592186264596 13194139533900 true] [17592186264595 1110 #uuid "bbf7d9ab-8258-5d0c-b997-6f5651d1d1a4" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264596 1034 "\\frac{(5\\ln(6)-\\ln(5))}{4\\ln(5)-7\\ln(6)}" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264596 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533900 true] [17592186264596 1111 #uuid "f91695cd-31c2-5dd8-a3bc-8c8d39866e0d" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264597 1017 #edb/ref 17592186264598 13194139533900 true] [17592186264597 1089 "q-66792" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264597 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533900 true] [17592186264597 1100 "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, what value of $x$ satisfies the equation ${e}^{x}={2}^{x+1}?$" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264597 1113 #uuid "d0e7f287-adec-5973-9d8d-d6bf16f0de13" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264597 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & ={2}^{x+1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{x+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{x+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =(x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x(1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264599 13194139533900 true] [17592186264598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264600 13194139533900 true] [17592186264598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264601 13194139533900 true] [17592186264598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264602 13194139533900 true] [17592186264598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264603 13194139533900 true] [17592186264598 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533900 true] [17592186264598 1041 "selection" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264598 1104 #edb/ref 17592186264599 13194139533900 true] [17592186264598 1110 #uuid "de46083e-cd07-56ed-bc00-6d359161d91d" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264599 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533900 true] [17592186264599 1111 #uuid "e1cd8fd1-719a-53f2-8250-2dd6f52b9fe9" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264600 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533900 true] [17592186264600 1111 #uuid "a7591086-c099-5a10-b96b-1e1751faf87e" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264601 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264601 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533900 true] [17592186264601 1111 #uuid "59c2d403-f4c5-512b-b9e4-67a2be33dcbb" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264602 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533900 true] [17592186264602 1111 #uuid "315db262-e025-5508-a5b1-5528a6e23f27" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264603 1034 "\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264603 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533900 true] [17592186264603 1111 #uuid "b349fc73-4e72-5c3d-b741-ad907e69d746" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264604 1017 #edb/ref 17592186264605 13194139533900 true] [17592186264604 1089 "q-66896" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264604 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533900 true] [17592186264604 1100 "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, what value of $x$ satisfies the equation ${e}^{x-1}={3}^{x}?$" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264604 1113 #uuid "4b29265f-c944-5a5b-bb00-edb60f6cc60f" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264604 1145 "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-1} & ={3}^{x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x-1}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-1 & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-1 & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ x-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 & =1 \\\\ x(1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264606 13194139533900 true] [17592186264605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264607 13194139533900 true] [17592186264605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264608 13194139533900 true] [17592186264605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264609 13194139533900 true] [17592186264605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264610 13194139533900 true] [17592186264605 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533900 true] [17592186264605 1041 "selection" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264605 1104 #edb/ref 17592186264607 13194139533900 true] [17592186264605 1110 #uuid "81d059f0-3026-5355-bdf0-ce4bfb21cd9c" 13194139533900 true] [17592186264606 1034 "\